{"uid":"45801c378359823f","name":"test_sh_reports_127_and_names_the_command_instead_of_raising","fullName":"tests.test_status_docker_absent_task080#test_sh_reports_127_and_names_the_command_instead_of_raising","historyId":"f655d59c3ac45b1c0cac885457d22065","time":{"start":1791891724370,"stop":1791891724372,"duration":2},"description":"Task 085's fix at the level it actually lives (steer 013 section 2,\n    #183): `sh()` itself, driven directly rather than through any one of its\n    callers, so the property every caller in `cli/main.py` inherits is pinned\n    in ONE place. `127` is deliberate and is the shell's own \"command not\n    found\" -- distinct from a 1-125 in-command failure and from a signal\n    death -- and the stderr must NAME the missing binary, since a caller that\n    surfaces that text is the only way an operator learns which binary was\n    absent. The absence is caused here (a name no `PATH` entry provides,\n    asserted), never inherited from the ambient host: this dev container\n    carries a real docker client.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 085's fix at the level it actually lives (steer 013 section 2,<br />\n#183): <code>sh()</code> itself, driven directly rather than through any one of its<br />\ncallers, so the property every caller in <code>cli/main.py</code> inherits is pinned<br />\nin ONE place. <code>127</code> is deliberate and is the shell's own &quot;command not<br />\nfound&quot; -- distinct from a 1-125 in-command failure and from a signal<br />\ndeath -- and the stderr must NAME the missing binary, since a caller that<br />\nsurfaces that text is the only way an operator learns which binary was<br />\nabsent. The absence is caused here (a name no <code>PATH</code> entry provides,<br />\nasserted), never inherited from the ambient host: this dev container<br />\ncarries a real docker client.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"bef